 "title": "What $100 will buy in 30 years (it's not $100) #shorts",
 "description": "At 3% inflation a year, $100 in cash buys about $74 of today's goods after 10 years, $55 after 20 and $41 after 30. To just keep up, that $100 has to grow to $134, $181 and $243.\n\nAssumptions: a steady 3% inflation rate every year (a round number; actual inflation changes year to year). The US Federal Reserve's longer-run goal is 2% inflation, measured by the PCE price index (source: federalreserve.gov); at 2%, $100 buys about $55 of today's goods after 30 years.\n\n#inflation #personalfinance #moneytips #savings #financialliteracy",
